{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1548622-the-end-of-a-moot","id":1548622,"title":"The End of a Moot","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-20T10:59:53-08:00","id":1548622,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> The End of a Moot","content":"Okay, I know the odds of me getting an answer to this are pretty slim, but I don't know where else to go. I'm talking about W:tA 4th/20th Anniversary and earlier editions here.<br /> <br /> At the end of a Moot, it's stated in many places that the Garou hold a revel. However, in some locations it's said that the Revel is the entirety of the sept hunting down enemies around the bawn and giving the Gnosis to the caern. But in other places, it's said the revel is hunting engling(s) -- in one place it says the englings possess prey animals, I think, but I can't remember where -- and the Gnosis generated goes to the individual Garou.<br /> <br /> But which one is right? I can't believe, 30 years later, that it was never clarified. Please help me. Or at least help me decide.<br /> <br /> (PS, if you have a source, tell me, and if I get an answer I'll reupload my W:tA spreadsheet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></span>","edited":{"userid":1765,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","user":"rderekp","date":".  Providing an incentive. 02-20-2025, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","name":"rderekp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T12:01:02-08:00","id":1548623,"title":"","content":"As ever, the most likely answer is \u201cDepends on the moot and the Sept in question\u201d - given the differences between the various tribal cultures (Not to mention within the several tribal subcultures) there are probably a number of possible approaches to the conduct of a Moot, from start to finish.<br /> <br /> Choose which one works for you and for the Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T12:45:20-08:00","id":1548628,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure where you're getting some of the things leading to some mechanical confusion.<br /> <br /> The donation of Gnosis to keep the Caern sanctified happens during monthly Sept Moots (held if nothing else for this specific reason). It's a function of the Moot Rite traditionally performed by the Master of the Howl to start the Moot, and the Gnosis donations can happen whenever as the Moot proceeds. This function isn't part of the other kinds of Moots, since they're generally more ad hoc and don't happen regularly to see to a Caern's spiritual needs.<br /> <br /> Hunting Englings is something some Septs arrange because the Gnosis costs ( x5 the level of the Caern) can be pretty steep and Garou don't regain Gnosis without specific effort. So having some Englings to refresh the Gnosis of the Sept is a practical matter to make sure upkeeping the Caern doesn't overtax the Garou living there. This is not official part of the Revel, but it's own even called the Sacred Hunt; though some Septs might combine them.<br /> <br /> Citations-<br /> <br /> W20 p56, 57: Describes the different types of Moots and their functions, Tribal variations, and discusses Revelry in its own subsection including that many times it just isn't done after a Moot.<br /> <br /> W20 p146: Details how Englings factor into Moots and the Sacred Hunt<br /> <br /> W20 p206: Details the Moot Rite itself, and how Gnosis is donated to the Caern<br /> <br /> If you look through those write-ups you'll see there's no assumption of the Revel itself being when Gnosis is offered up to the Caern, or when Garou do the Sacred Hunt to replenish their person Gnosis pools. Just that the traditional Revel involves hunting enemies and threats to the Sept, but the specifics vary wildly based on Tribe and practical concerns. I obviously can't cite a passage that doesn't exist, but nothing in W20 says the Gnosis/Englings are part of the Revel... so there's nothing the books need to clarify here as they don't contradict themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T13:33:32-08:00","id":1548632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rderekp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1548622-the-end-of-a-moot#post1548622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I know the odds of me getting an answer to this are pretty slim, but I don't know where else to go. I'm talking about W:tA 4th/20th Anniversary and earlier editions here.<br /> <br /> At the end of a Moot, it's stated in many places that the Garou hold a revel. However, in some locations it's said that the Revel is the entirety of the sept hunting down enemies around the bawn and giving the Gnosis to the caern. But in other places, it's said the revel is hunting engling(s) -- in one place it says the englings possess prey animals, I think, but I can't remember where -- and the Gnosis generated goes to the individual Garou.<br /> <br /> But which one is right? I can't believe, 30 years later, that it was never clarified. Please help me. Or at least help me decide.<br /> <br /> (PS, if you have a source, tell me, and if I get an answer I'll reupload my W:tA spreadsheet).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this depends on the moot and sept. Lets say its Corporate wolves. Just as an example. Their meetings are inside their businesses. What are they going to do? Kill janitors? No. Most likely their revel involves cute secretaries and liberal amounts of alcohol. Lets say its Fiana, in a caern which is a Pub where &quot;Everybody knows your name&quot;. Once again, whom are they going to kill? Various ghetto trash who came too close to their pub? Yeah, that's smart, lets attract police/technocracy/NWO attention to our caern. Use common sense. All of those Garou may go to umbra and kill few banes who wondered to close to their caerns, IN UMBRA. But highly unlikely to go and start exterminating someone with extreme prejudice in real world. Which brings me to another interesting conundrum. Does it even makes a difference? &quot;The evil that men do&quot; doesn't only &quot;Lives on and on&quot; but attracts banes. Killing a bane will NOT stop men from doing evil. The only thing that stops humans from doing evil is taking HIM out. Not a bane. What is primal? Bane or &quot;Evil that men do&quot; (which &quot;lives on and on&quot;, if you got the reference - Good, if not, I feel bad for you<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. In any case. Use common sence. It is unlikely for the garou to go on killing spree in urban areas where there are cops and cameras in most places. The possible exception are &quot;Hood&quot; of Bone Gnawers. They can do the same &quot;Blood vs Crips&quot; in the game without fear of police (Same as they do IRL). UP with Six, Down Five. F.O.O.L.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26712-tigerclaw_x","name":"Tigerclaw_x","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T14:23:51-08:00","id":1548633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1548622-the-end-of-a-moot?p=1548628#post1548628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure where you're getting some of the things leading to some mechanical confusion.<br /> <br /> The donation of Gnosis to keep the Caern sanctified happens during monthly Sept Moots (held if nothing else for this specific reason). It's a function of the Moot Rite traditionally performed by the Master of the Howl to start the Moot, and the Gnosis donations can happen whenever as the Moot proceeds. This function isn't part of the other kinds of Moots, since they're generally more ad hoc and don't happen regularly to see to a Caern's spiritual needs.<br /> <br /> Hunting Englings is something some Septs arrange because the Gnosis costs ( x5 the level of the Caern) can be pretty steep and Garou don't regain Gnosis without specific effort. So having some Englings to refresh the Gnosis of the Sept is a practical matter to make sure upkeeping the Caern doesn't overtax the Garou living there. This is not official part of the Revel, but it's own even called the Sacred Hunt; though some Septs might combine them.<br /> <br /> Citations-<br /> <br /> W20 p56, 57: Describes the different types of Moots and their functions, Tribal variations, and discusses Revelry in its own subsection including that many times it just isn't done after a Moot.<br /> <br /> W20 p146: Details how Englings factor into Moots and the Sacred Hunt<br /> <br /> W20 p206: Details the Moot Rite itself, and how Gnosis is donated to the Caern<br /> <br /> If you look through those write-ups you'll see there's no assumption of the Revel itself being when Gnosis is offered up to the Caern, or when Garou do the Sacred Hunt to replenish their person Gnosis pools. Just that the traditional Revel involves hunting enemies and threats to the Sept, but the specifics vary wildly based on Tribe and practical concerns. I obviously can't cite a passage that doesn't exist, but nothing in W20 says the Gnosis/Englings are part of the Revel... so there's nothing the books need to clarify here as they don't contradict themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the answer I was looking for. I admit my confusion. When it says moots in the book, I assume it means the monthly moot unless it specifies otherwise, and it seems I may be wrong about that. Honestly, I don't know how I missed p. 57 except maybe my brain just holds verbiage from older editions or something.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I think what confused me in the first place is how the Sacred Hunt isn't mentioned in the section on the Moot. Not in W20 or any of the previous books, as far as I can tell. But then, I have a lot of them and get overwhelmed sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></span>","edited":{"userid":1765,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","user":"rderekp","date":". 02-20-2025, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","name":"rderekp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T18:34:17-08:00","id":1548648,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Sacred Hunt tends to be in the Gnosis section, and referenced as being in Moots there, but the Moot sections usually don't mention it.<br /> <br /> Another point of disconnect is that the &quot;story&quot; parts of the books tend to focus more on Hearing Moots (as they tend to bracket PC activity by being a narrative device for both kicking off a plot and reporting the outcomes), while the &quot;rules&quot; parts tend to focus on the Sept Moots. This makes sense as a Hearing is usually a narrative push towards whatever the actual thing the players are going to do, while the Sept Moot is treated as something to do in and of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T23:07:03-08:00","id":1548657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rderekp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1548622-the-end-of-a-moot?p=1548633#post1548633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what confused me in the first place is how the Sacred Hunt isn't mentioned in the section on the Moot. Not in W20 or any of the previous books, as far as I can tell. But then, I have a lot of them and get overwhelmed sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the same problem as you long ago. Unfortunately a lot of things concerning moots, caerns, certain rites, and other key topics are scattered all over the place in Werewolf (sometimes between multiple sourcebooks). It's not always clear how things are supposed to be run. Instead of consolidating these tidbits together in one section in the next version of the corebook, they just keep repeating the existing divisions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T06:09:32-08:00","id":1548672,"title":"","content":"Possibly because the subject always seems to be moot \u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}